# Cloudflare Pages proxy (rewrite, HTTP 200 = same-origin proxy, NOT a 30x).
#
# The React app calls RELATIVE paths (axios baseURL '/api', bare '/auth/refresh')
# that rely on the Vite dev proxy. Pages is static with no proxy, so these
# rewrites forward the browser's same-origin /api and /auth calls to the Render
# API. Because the browser still sees them as same-origin, no CORS preflight and
# no frontend code change are needed.
#
# >>> REPLACE the placeholder host below with your real Render URL <<<
# (from the Render dashboard, e.g. https://grw-api.onrender.com).
# Order matters: most specific first. Cloudflare uses the FIRST match.
/api/*   https://grw-api.onrender.com/api/:splat    200
/auth/*  https://grw-api.onrender.com/auth/:splat   200

# NOTE: WebSocket / socket.io is intentionally NOT proxied here — Pages
# _redirects cannot upgrade to a WS tunnel. This is acceptable in paper mode
# (LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=false): there is no live market feed to stream, so the
# real-time socket is not required for sign-up / login / subscribe / dashboard.

# SPA fallback: every non-asset, non-proxied path serves index.html so
# react-router client routes (/login, /dashboard, ...) resolve on hard refresh.
/*  /index.html  200
